        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a$ decreases by approximately $13.0\\%$.",
          "worked": "Write $a=\\frac{k}{b}$. When $b$ becomes $1.15b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{k}{1.15b}\\\\a_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{20}{23}a.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage decrease is\n$$\\left(1-\\frac{20}{23}\\right)\\times100\\%=\\frac{300}{23}\\%\\approx13.0\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "decreased by $12\\%$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a$ increases by approximately $13.6\\%$.",
          "worked": "Write $a=\\frac{k}{b}$. When $b$ becomes $0.88b$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{k}{0.88b}\\\\a_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{25}{22}a.\\end{align*}$$\nThe percentage increase is\n$$\\left(\\frac{25}{22}-1\\right)\\times100\\%=\\frac{150}{11}\\%\\approx13.6\\%.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
